#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087511 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "c7cc2dca-cc41-561c-bc48-bbcda272dd71" :question/math-academy-id "e-5792" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/assets/1c498dcdef2a71cc27117c2c0a43dd54074128ec3e5693e13a12d18b660d1cf4.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${\\color{black}x_1= 2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_{2,3}=-2\\pm \\textrm{i}}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=1}.$ \n\nTherefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}-x(-2-\\text{i})-x(-2+\\text{i})+(-2+\\text{i})(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}+4x+5) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+5x-2{x}^{2}-8x-10 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-3x-10 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x) = x^3+2x^2-3x-10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087586 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "92ac2f4f-d0a5-5ccb-9213-87495927ccb8" :question/math-academy-id "e-8799" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=x_2=2,x_3=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${\\color{black}x_1=x_2=2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_3=1},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=3},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1) & =3({x}^{2}-4x+4)(x-1) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}+4x+4x-4) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+8x-4) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}+24x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = 3x^3 -15x^2+24x-12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7d017c2-e3ff-56d9-9334-9ac4fa843657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-19x+30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304686} {:answer/id #uuid "3c61eea0-6b09-573a-b969-b636455c3741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}-38x-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304687} {:answer/id #uuid "151c154c-d125-5381-9ace-152bee787a80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+47x+60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304688} {:answer/id #uuid "e58c95f7-87e5-56a0-956d-88829d4e8f33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+19x+60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304689} {:answer/id #uuid "1ceb7ee0-935f-5b83-9144-6119f5574980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ceb7ee0-935f-5b83-9144-6119f5574980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304690} :answer-field/id #uuid "753ec0e2-b325-5183-8e84-914a8d2e5340" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304685}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5046e0c1-2f8b-58f5-a21d-913e91899338" :question/math-academy-id "q-104467" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{2}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=-3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-1.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{1}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=-3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-1(x-(-5))(x-(-4))(x-(-3)) \\\\  & =-(x+5)(x+4)(x+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(x+5)(x+4)(x+3) & =-({x}^{2}+9x+20)(x+3) \\\\  & =-({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+9{x}^{2}+27x+20x+60) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087915 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae36425f-5e48-5d4f-8932-3a137c1f94e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x^{3} - 8x^{2} + 10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084502} {:answer/id #uuid "e7f7b873-fb65-5a93-bedf-1b8d8b3b6cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x^{3} + 4x^{2} + 10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084503} {:answer/id #uuid "154b65e5-ff43-514f-b226-ec2977e6cc3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} - 4x^{2} - 10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084504} {:answer/id #uuid "20ed9f7e-6cd2-5097-861e-c62eb98176d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} + 8x^{2} + 5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084505} {:answer/id #uuid "291c4f7d-5ed3-53a3-8a1a-28b5bab60d35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x^{3} + 4x^{2} - 5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae36425f-5e48-5d4f-8932-3a137c1f94e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x^{3} - 8x^{2} + 10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084502} :answer-field/id #uuid "159db6ae-8ceb-5e94-ae54-fd52d97b24a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b7607d8-f365-578e-840c-7619cca90194" :question/math-academy-id "q-104469" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{1}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-2(x-(-5))(x-0)(x-1) \\\\  & =-2x(x+5)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x(x+5)(x-1) & =-2x({x}^{2}+4x-5) \\\\  & =-2({x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8304950d-6419-57c7-9abe-14caec07459d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+50x+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304693} {:answer/id #uuid "908682db-2b13-5c2b-bf37-704b0d1db340" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+20x-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304694} {:answer/id #uuid "3f46aa04-1eae-5968-925a-f7fde1628daf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+50x-150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304695} {:answer/id #uuid "381bf829-01de-5bda-b8ca-3b1a094b4d6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+50x+150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304696} {:answer/id #uuid "7eb85c7a-b314-5c83-b299-1b58b61fea34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+25x-75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f46aa04-1eae-5968-925a-f7fde1628daf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+50x-150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304695} :answer-field/id #uuid "94559dc5-1453-5aed-9198-b151af7188a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f062701-62d1-5aa3-83ee-10a91ad72608" :question/math-academy-id "q-107669" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=3,{x}_{2,3}=\\pm 5\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =2(x-3)(x-5\\text{i})(x-(-5\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2(x-3)(x-5\\text{i})(x+5\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-3)(x-5\\text{i})(x+5\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 2(x-3)({x}^{2}-(5\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 2(x-3)({x}^{2}+25) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+25x-75) & = \\\\ 2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+50x-150 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+50x-150.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af094840-468d-54c0-b013-c15534112a19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+16x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304700} {:answer/id #uuid "240e3f0e-d70e-5a16-8c55-f76e7e83e4d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304701} {:answer/id #uuid "21b6a9b3-baef-5315-b1b9-da739f1d1a46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304702} {:answer/id #uuid "01cd5c5a-cd6b-5097-b524-14a8b4624aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+32x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304703} {:answer/id #uuid "1207e264-c672-5dcb-bfe4-eaa0a7ca73bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01cd5c5a-cd6b-5097-b524-14a8b4624aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+32x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304703} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d86a62f-bd17-5303-ba04-3f9325c1e31c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "78253fad-7e11-5fbb-92d7-9defd14f1c64" :question/math-academy-id "q-107670" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/assets/a926400e24bc00ca9027d44461e800fa22015ff8289f05fba3a8b51f8b72cce5.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $4.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=0$ and ${x}_{2,3}=2\\pm 2\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=4.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =4(x-0)(x-(2+2\\text{i}))(x-(2-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =4x(x-(2+2\\text{i}))(x-(2-2\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x(x-(2+2\\text{i}))(x-(2-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-x(2-2\\text{i})-x(2+2\\text{i})+(2+2\\text{i})(2-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-4x+8) & = \\\\ 4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+32x & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+32x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd7b13fb-b445-5fe2-bff8-ad254883cc83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+8x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304707} {:answer/id #uuid "86941038-ebe7-5c3e-af46-5e8d3a2057c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+5x+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304708} {:answer/id #uuid "3dc5df4b-1d30-5a54-b5a2-e23d08ba0010" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+x+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304709} {:answer/id #uuid "d43578ed-8490-57e6-ae17-c39bbd98e882" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+11x+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304710} {:answer/id #uuid "bd93bce9-90d4-5262-84cc-f961bf702490" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+11x+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d43578ed-8490-57e6-ae17-c39bbd98e882" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+11x+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304710} :answer-field/id #uuid "955d8a49-776c-576a-a999-54912f95df8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304706}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b622ddf-d8be-54e3-8391-21ca3422a7bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-107681" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-1,$ ${x}_{2}=4,$ and ${x}_{3}=5,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-1,$ ${x}_{1}=4,$ and ${x}_{3}=5,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =1(x-(-1))(x-4)(x-5) \\\\  & =(x+1)(x-4)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)(x-4)(x-5) & =({x}^{2}-3x-4)(x-5) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-5{x}^{2}+15x-4x+20 \\\\  & ={x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+11x+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+11x+20.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278535 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27a51973-2aaf-59d1-bfad-18627b7ab64f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278537} {:answer/id #uuid "7d6e2840-e270-59a4-8d60-c00f23f258ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278538} {:answer/id #uuid "56171563-0615-5fb3-b854-9300e0b02d03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278539} {:answer/id #uuid "ef6e91be-e836-5466-8026-ab7735b0b298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278540} {:answer/id #uuid "a4bd8db2-376d-5ea8-89f5-d2d2a68965c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27a51973-2aaf-59d1-bfad-18627b7ab64f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278537} :answer-field/id #uuid "9da7061c-555a-54eb-aa9f-d21b81deaa88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "54688a98-1474-5993-a7d9-b3966da03d6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-17407" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/assets/b771ac7e3d7e724b1eae9ebfc592d36a903a1fc46cc2aac5a55ea9517dc2ce12.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a cubic polynomial $f(x).$\nFind $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =1(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x-(-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i}) & = \\\\ (x-4)({x}^{2}-x(-3\\text{i})-x(3\\text{i})+(3\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-4)({x}^{2}+9) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+9x-4{x}^{2}-36 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304712 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b56a55e-d4af-5687-91dc-04572d49c2b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304714} {:answer/id #uuid "6dbc2343-c979-5b18-acec-fd84e1825aa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304715} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c38465-c21c-58c9-acd5-a25476701397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+24x-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304716} {:answer/id #uuid "2e7eaece-6d5d-5c70-82e6-cea9c43ee928" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+25x-39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304717} {:answer/id #uuid "317ba80a-9e77-5435-b0f1-96272cbd372b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e7eaece-6d5d-5c70-82e6-cea9c43ee928" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+25x-39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304717} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0b69fc7-7644-53a8-9834-af1d6c37a7db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304713}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "30239ac5-d2ec-5338-817c-8dbb2bd8190d" :question/math-academy-id "q-17408" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/assets/75fab7d9a7b9aabdd19a769384c548b033a3d8d30879bf647d6e8852c7b3ba9a.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2,3}=2\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =1(x-3)(x-(2+3\\text{i}))(x-(2-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-3)(x-(2+3\\text{i}))(x-(2-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)(x-(2+3\\text{i}))(x-(2-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-3)({x}^{2}-x(2-3\\text{i})-x(2+3\\text{i})+(2+3\\text{i})(2-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-3)({x}^{2}-4x+13) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+13x-3{x}^{2}+12x-39 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+25x-39 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+25x-39.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304719 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90eebe8d-a1bf-5a93-9fe5-6679ea8bcebf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304721} {:answer/id #uuid "0635812a-7fa1-5e30-8c2a-bc2d9a42e2a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90eebe8d-a1bf-5a93-9fe5-6679ea8bcebf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304721} :answer-field/id #uuid "594494cb-8751-5c20-8e29-9125c06203c8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304720} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a4473db-7fee-5b1f-8a26-047e5fd0e3dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a4473db-7fee-5b1f-8a26-047e5fd0e3dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304724} :answer-field/id #uuid "787cb405-e289-5a06-b049-1dc9f7c5ad39" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304723} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c852974-a27c-5abc-be39-2ca651f2d7bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c852974-a27c-5abc-be39-2ca651f2d7bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304726} :answer-field/id #uuid "2841aef9-c21a-5455-ae6f-554f7030f20e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304725} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e68c843-f27c-5e49-9298-c55dab376cf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e68c843-f27c-5e49-9298-c55dab376cf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304728} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8078909-afdc-5bb3-ac92-eb797b3038df" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304727}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef6eba9d-6395-5176-8a97-4f77fe2fd73d" :question/math-academy-id "q-316617" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-4,$ ${x}_{2}=1,$ and ${x}_{3}=2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-4,$ ${x}_{2}=1,$ and ${x}_{3}=2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =3(x-(-4))(x-1)(x-2) \\\\  & =3(x+4)(x-1)(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+4)(x-1)(x-2) & =3({x}^{2}+3x-4)(x-2) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-6x-4x+8) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-10x+8) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-30x+24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-30x+24.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4c645a7-6e88-5972-b95f-905dac795ff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4c645a7-6e88-5972-b95f-905dac795ff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281848} :answer-field/id #uuid "91791d0a-1066-5c42-b09c-9cb09d183694" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281847} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10c26c3e-2747-5197-ad23-a2ed18872e4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10c26c3e-2747-5197-ad23-a2ed18872e4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281850} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bac3080-51d6-5bbf-b341-0d56be3ea619" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281849} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "760a6ca5-e3eb-547b-b1ce-767c2123969f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "760a6ca5-e3eb-547b-b1ce-767c2123969f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281852} :answer-field/id #uuid "20b89ba4-b596-516d-8f05-c3c0e495998e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281851} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2933e7f1-ebb8-52f6-b1b0-a983d26a9cc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2933e7f1-ebb8-52f6-b1b0-a983d26a9cc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281854} :answer-field/id #uuid "40817d4a-1275-5ff8-aef6-04cef1d3a688" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b79b1845-4a56-5456-a000-eb06d5845200" :question/math-academy-id "q-316621" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-4,{x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-4,$ ${x}_{2}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-(-4))(x-(-4))(x-1) \\\\  & =2(x+4)(x+4)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+4)(x+4)(x-1) & =2({x}^{2}+8x+16)(x-1) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+8{x}^{2}-8x+16x-16) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}+8x-16) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}+16x-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}+16x-32.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7193273d-34dc-56fc-a691-019429bdc7ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304731} {:answer/id #uuid "bf138c3b-e186-5c39-8b74-ee1bbc10e18d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7193273d-34dc-56fc-a691-019429bdc7ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304731} :answer-field/id #uuid "78cb8ffb-41ec-5e65-9588-6ef2643e0a3f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8dac704-a25a-5713-9310-0fa3fdb91d80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8dac704-a25a-5713-9310-0fa3fdb91d80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304734} :answer-field/id #uuid "8920c028-f8ad-508f-95a2-bb7c30b5ead7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304733} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18303a81-f79d-5f7b-8258-a416fa4e7e3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18303a81-f79d-5f7b-8258-a416fa4e7e3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304736} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7843f6e-45f2-5168-8080-8d196290edab" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304735} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1d50193-c05c-5c45-9de0-43cdbeb19830" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1d50193-c05c-5c45-9de0-43cdbeb19830" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304738} :answer-field/id #uuid "36ef6687-5c3e-515d-a33a-d86d7a4a65de" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5f5cc839-e6a4-52c2-9f56-171a4dee9b16" :question/math-academy-id "q-316689" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/assets/b2dbc407d70f4e6d3cf35dd24e1a6fb7d463207631a0498595ed40550ac86433.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a cubic polynomial $f(x).$\nFind $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $-5.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 2\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-5.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-5(x-3)(x-2\\text{i})(x-(-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =-5(x-3)(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5(x-3)(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i}) & = \\\\ -5(x-3)({x}^{2}+x(2\\text{i})-x(2\\text{i})-(2\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ -5(x-3)({x}^{2}+4) & = \\\\ -5({x}^{3}+4x-3{x}^{2}-12) & = \\\\ -5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-20x+60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-20x+60.$"}]}
